- **Zombie sweper (line ~6954)**: `summary` is a fixed literal — safe. The PATCH interpolates `z.id` (numeric) and fixed strings. Actually wait, the summary contains no untrusted data. `z.name` is only used in DRY log. So this call site is SAFE (only ids + fixed text). Hmm, but the `-f "output[summary]=<fixed text>"` — fixed text with parens — inside double quotes... `output[summary]` in double quotes — parens inside double quotes are fine. OK safe.

- **Placeholder conclusion (line ~7060)**: `coverUrl` — from `coverRun.html_url || coverRun.url` — a GitHub-generated run URL. This is API-returned, and could in theory contain arbitrary data? html_url is `https://github.com/o/r/actions/runs/<id>` — GitHub-controlled. `url` is the API url. Low risk but still run-derived text interpolated into double quotes. Per the ticket's audit: "titles, comments, branch names" — details_url with coverUrl is run-derived. I should convert this one too — via shellQuote or the temp-file approach.

Hmm, wait. For PATCH endpoints the body would need the JSON approach as well, or single-quote escaping via shellQuote. The ticket says: "convert them the same way or to single-quote escaping via one helper `shellQuote()`".

- **dispatchCiWorkflow (line ~2552)**: `--ref ' + branchName` — UNQUOTED branch name (PR head ref — untrusted!). This one is dangerous: `gh workflow run quality.yml --repo o/r --ref <branch>` — a branch name like `a$(reboot)` or `a;rm -rf /` executes. Actually is branchName validated upstream? Let me check where branch names come from — the PR head ref from the GitHub API. PRs can have branch names with weird chars (git ref names permit shell metacharacters, as the comment at line 3892 notes). The ghost dispatch at 3892 already single-quote-escapes `ticket.branch`. The `dispatchCiWorkflow` should use shellQuote too.

- **silentUpdateCommand (line ~2184)**: `--branch ' + branchName` — branchName unquoted, inside a `bash -c "..."`? Let me look at the full silentUpdateCommand builder. Note there's also `pushTarget` with the branch name at the end. And `stderrFile` sanitized. Let me read the builder.

- **Line 1064 local runner**: ticketKey/projectKey/baseBranch — from Jira/config. Ticket keys are like "PROJ-123" — trusted-ish. baseBranch from config. encodedConfigFile is a temp path built by code. Lower risk; out of ticket scope? The ticket says "PR/run-derived text" — ticket keys are not PR/run-derived. Skip.

